    <dcterms:title>Round the Sofa</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_the_Sofa</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>David Price, Vanessa Mosher, Jennifer Lee, Alev Akman, Andy Wallace, Audrey Emmitt and Eugenia Corbo</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Round the Sofa" by Elizabeth Cleghorn Gaskell is a two-volume collection published in 1859. A narrator provides the framework as various storytellers gather around a sofa, each sharing their tale. The collection includes the novel "My Lady Ludlow" and five short stories with diverse themes. This framing device connects otherwise disparate narratives, creating an intimate atmosphere of shared storytelling among companions. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 73.6 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
